我看见它们初次冒出来，也看见第一批花瓣落下。

11
00:00:50,081 --> 00:00:56,000
I've noticed a difference in how overgrown the hedges are as suddenly everything comes to life.
我注意到树篱变得多么茂密，一切仿佛突然活了过来。

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,721
And the smells are different and like even the way the air tastes is different it's just incredible.
气味也不一样了，甚至连空气入口的感觉都不一样，实在太奇妙了。

13
00:01:02,721 --> 00:01:09,270
And being able to observe those my new changes is something I never gave myself the space to do.
能够观察这些细微变化，是我以前从未给自己留出空间去做的事。my new 处识别存疑。

14
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:18,471
And these morning walks do you give me that space and I think it just makes me so much more attentive to nature and makes me more grateful for nature.
这些晨间散步确实给了我这样的空间。我想，这让我更关注自然，也更感激自然。do you give 处含混。

15
00:01:18,481 --> 00:01:22,081
That is definitely something really really positive that's come out of lockdown for me.
这绝对是封锁期间给我带来的一个非常非常积极的变化。

16
00:01:22,081 --> 00:01:25,521
Because I just didn't give myself that slow pace of life before.
因为在这之前，我根本没有让自己这样放慢生活节奏。

17
00:01:25,521 --> 00:01:31,830
Especially in spring like the coming of spring is a beautiful thing but it's always been my least favorite season because.
尤其是春天，春天的到来很美好，但它一直是我最不喜欢的季节，因为……

18
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:40,801
Due to exam season I was always too stressed with academics to really look outside and see what was happening to the world but I did that this year.
因为考试季，我总为学业太焦虑，没能好好望向窗外，看看世界正在发生什么。但今年我做到了。

19
00:01:40,801 --> 00:01:52,071
If you can go on a walk every morning then do because I don't think you'll regret it.
如果你能每天早上去散步，就去吧，因为我想你不会后悔。

20
00:01:52,081 --> 00:02:00,471
See what I mean about it looking over green this was all paired back in the winter and now it's just brimming with life.
你们明白我说植物长得茂密是什么意思了吧？冬天这里都修剪过，如今却满是生机。over green、paired back 处待核。

21
00:02:00,481 --> 00:02:06,071
Also controversial opinion thistles are beautiful weeds my mum and I always say this.
还有个可能有争议的看法：蓟是很美的野草。我和妈妈总这么说。

22
00:02:06,081 --> 00:02:10,560
She actually in her vegetable patch has the most incredible massive thistle.
其实她的菜地里就有一株特别惊人、特别大的蓟。

23
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:15,351
I know they're supposed to be a weed but they're just so beautiful this field is particularly gorgeous.
我知道它们被当成杂草，但它们真的很美。这片田野尤其漂亮。

24
00:02:15,361 --> 00:02:20,880
There is fellow walker coming so I probably won't continue talking to you just for now.
有另一位散步的人过来了，所以我暂时可能就不继续跟你们说话了。

25
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:27,431
Um that I'm going to enjoy my walk be present be mindful not listen to music or anything at the moment.
嗯，我会享受散步，专注当下，静静感受，暂时不听音乐或其他东西。that 处衔接含混。

26
00:02:27,441 --> 00:03:03,271
And I will show you some beautiful things that I see if I see anything particularly gorgeous like more thistles ah there are so many.
如果看见特别漂亮的东西，我会拍给你们看，比如更多的蓟。啊，真有好多。

27
00:03:03,281 --> 00:03:08,801
In my bag with me I don't bring very much at all but I'll show you what I usually bring.
我包里其实没带多少东西，不过我给你们看看平时带什么。

28
00:03:08,801 --> 00:03:14,001
Sometimes I ring a picnic rug I didn't today because I wasn't planning on sitting down even though I kind of regret that now.
有时我会带野餐垫。今天没带，因为我本来没打算坐下，不过现在有点后悔了。ring 疑似识别错误。

29
00:03:14,001 --> 00:03:16,310
Just bring my phone in case there's an emergency.
就带上手机，以防万一有紧急情况。

30
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:19,200
I bring my headphones even though I don't always end up using them.
我会带耳机，虽然最后并不总会用上。

31
